<BaseLayout title="Differential" description="Differential options including Ford 8.8 IRS for high-horsepower LS Genesis Coupe builds.">
  <h1>Differential</h1>
  <p>
    The stock Gen Coupe differential is fine for moderate power. For high-horsepower builds, the Ford 8.8 IRS swap is the common upgrade.
  </p>

  <h2>High Horsepower Option: Ford 8.8 IRS</h2>
  <p>
    For builds targeting 1000+ hp, many people swap to a Ford 8.8 IRS differential. This requires custom axles from DSS.
    DSS needs your wheel hubs to broach them from 30-spline to 33-spline.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Drivers side axle length: ~23.25&quot; (closer to 23-3/8&quot;)</li>
    <li>Passenger side: ~24.25&quot; (closer to 24-3/8&quot;)</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Official measurements are taken from the wheel hub to the differential seal. See Jason Riddle’s documented 8.8 swaps and the DSS order examples in the community groups.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href="https://www.tiktok.com/t/ZTfag4jc8/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TikTok video of an 8.8 install</a>
  </p>

